%I A396728 #21 Sep 12 2026 15:01:21
%S A396728 2,3,5,17,127,5001,3201005
%N A396728 Number of antichains of subsets of an n-element set (Sperner families) that do not contain both a set and its complement.
%C A396728 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of cliques (including the empty clique) in the graph on {0, ..., 2^n - 1} in which x ~ y iff x and y are incomparable as bitmasks and y != x XOR (2^n - 1); i.e., the incomparability graph of B_n with the complementation matching removed.
%H A396728 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sperner_family">Sperner family</a>.
%F A396728 a(n) <= A000372(n).
%F A396728 a(n) >= 2^binomial(n, (n-1)/2) for odd n, since the middle layer of B_n contains no complementary pair; a(n) >= 3^(binomial(n, n/2)/2) for even n.
%F A396728 log_2(a(n)) ~ binomial(n, floor(n/2)) ~ 2^n * sqrt(2/(Pi*n)).
%F A396728 a(n) >= A169974(n) = A306020(n) + 1 for odd n, since no level of B_n contains a complementary pair when n is odd; equality for n = 1 and n = 3.
%e A396728 For n = 2 the 6 antichains counted by A000372(2) are {}, {{}}, {{x}}, {{y}}, {{x,y}} and {{x},{y}}. The last is excluded since {x} and {y} are complementary, so a(2) = 5.
%e A396728 Also the Sierpinski gasket can be seen by plotting the submask relation x incomparable y:
%e A396728   n=1    n=2     n=3
%e A396728   ##     ####    ########
%e A396728   .#     .#.#    .#.#.#.#
%e A396728          ..##    ..##..##
%e A396728          ...#    ...#...#
%e A396728                  ....####
%e A396728                  .....#.#
%e A396728                  ......##
%e A396728                  .......#
%e A396728 The # marks where x incomparable y (submask relation), producing the Kronecker-power Sierpinski pattern. Each quadrant recursively mirrors the previous stage, with the lower-left quadrant empty.
%o A396728 (Python)
%o A396728 def a(n):
%o A396728     l = 1 << n; u = l - 1
%o A396728     def count(C):
%o A396728         t,m = 1,len(C)
%o A396728         for i in range(m):
%o A396728             x = C[i]
%o A396728             t += count([y for y in C[i+1:] if y != (u ^ x) and (x & ~y) and (y & ~x)])
%o A396728         return t
%o A396728     return count(list(range(l)))
%Y A396728 Cf. A000372, A001047, A001206, A003182, A006126, A007363, A014466, A016269, A169974, A306020.
%K A396728 nonn,hard,more,new
